  "track.storage.m.choose.overview": "The ClinicBook app has five kinds of data: 500 appointments, a few settings, a profile photo, a lab-results PDF, and a draft note. Each needs a different home. To choose, we ask up to four questions in turn. The first question answered \"yes\" decides where the data goes.",
  "track.storage.m.choose.wrapup": "Where data goes follows what the data is, not habit. What the user wants to keep and open in other apps goes to shared storage. What can be downloaded again goes to the cache. A few small settings go to DataStore. Many records you filter and edit go to Room. Everything else is an app-specific file.\nA wrong choice does not fail at once. It shows up later: as the list grows, when the device runs out of space, or when the user uninstalls.\nPicture a house: a fridge for food that spoils, a safe for papers, a bookshelf for things you look up. Putting things in the wrong place does not break anything today, but it hurts sooner or later.",
