  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s1.title": "Open a FileOutputStream: draft.txt drops to 0 bytes",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s1.explain": "Opening a FileOutputStream without append mode truncates the old contents the moment it opens, before a single byte is written. From here on, the old draft is no longer on disk.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.direct.s1": "Open a FileOutputStream: draft.txt drops to 0 bytes",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s2.title": "Half of the new draft is written",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s2.explain": "The 40 KB draft is being written; the first 20 KB are on disk. If all goes well, it finishes in a few milliseconds.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.direct.s2": "Half of the new draft is written",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s3.title": "The process is killed mid-write",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s3.explain": "The app is in the background, memory is short, the system kills the process. No chance to run finally or close the stream. Half of the new file is on disk; the old version was lost at step 1.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.direct.s3": "The process is killed mid-write",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s4.title": "Reopen the app: half a draft is read",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.direct.s4.explain": "readText returns the first 20 KB without complaint. If the file is JSON, parsing throws; if it is text, the user sees a truncated draft with no idea why.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.direct.s4": "Reopen the app: half a draft is read",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s1.title": "startWrite: writing to draft.txt.new",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s1.explain": "AtomicFile does not touch draft.txt. It opens a new file named draft.txt.new and returns that file's stream.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.atomic.s1": "startWrite: writing to draft.txt.new",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s2.title": "Half the draft is written to the .new file",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s2.explain": "draft.txt is still the complete old version; half of the new one sits in draft.txt.new.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.atomic.s2": "Half the draft is written to the .new file",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s3.title": "The process is killed mid-write",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s3.explain": "The same kill as before. finishWrite never ran, so no rename happened; the original file was never touched.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.atomic.s3": "The process is killed mid-write",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s4.title": "Reopen the app: the complete old version is read",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.atomic.s4.explain": "readFully reads draft.txt: the version before the last edit. The user loses exactly the edit being written, not the whole draft, and the file is never half-written.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.atomic.s4": "Reopen the app: the complete old version is read",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s1.title": "Download the results PDF into cacheDir",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s1.explain": "The first time the lab results are opened, the app downloads a 2 MB PDF and saves it in cacheDir so it opens instantly next time.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.cache.s1": "Download the results PDF into cacheDir",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s2.title": "Space runs low: the system deletes cache files",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s2.explain": "Days later the user records a long video and internal storage is nearly full. The system deletes files from apps' caches to reclaim space; the app is not told.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.cache.s2": "Space runs low: the system deletes cache files",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s3.title": "Open the file as is: FileNotFoundException",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s3.explain": "The app assumes the file is still there and opens it. It is gone: opening throws FileNotFoundException and the results screen shows an error.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.cache.s3": "Open the file as is: FileNotFoundException",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s4.title": "Check first, download again if missing",
  "track.storage.m.file.s.cache.s4.explain": "Check exists() before reading; if it is missing, download it again. The user waits for one more download and sees no error.",
  "track.storage.m.file.ev.cache.s4": "Check first, download again if missing",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.try": "Walk all four steps of each case; watch the \"Disk\" row.",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.direct.s2": "Nothing is wrong at this step. The trouble is that the old version was gone the moment the stream opened, so the whole write is a window of danger.",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.direct.s3": "A dead process runs no more code, so no cleanup can happen. Every write must assume it can be cut off at any byte.",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.direct.s4": "Reading a half-written file raises no error: readText returns whatever bytes are on disk. The failure only shows when parsing, or when the user reads it.",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.atomic.s2": "The Android docs say: it writes to a new file with \".new\" appended, and only then renames it over the original. [[src:ax-atomicfile]]",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.atomic.s3": "finishWrite is when the stream is closed, synced to disk and renamed. Until then the original file is untouched. [[src:ax-atomicfile]]",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.atomic.s4": "Renaming over an existing name is atomic on Linux: there is no moment when the target name is missing. A reader sees the old version or the new one, never half of one. [[src:man-rename]]",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.cache.s2": "The Android docs say: when the device is low on internal storage, Android may delete cache files to reclaim space. [[src:ax-app-specific]]",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.cache.s3": "The same docs say: check that a cache file exists before reading it. [[src:ax-app-specific]]",
  "track.storage.m.file.co.cache.s4": "The cache is only for things you can get back. Checking and downloading again turns a deleted file into a short wait, not an error. [[src:ax-app-specific]]",
