  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s1.title": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s1.explain": "The user skipped version 2. clinic.db on the device says version 1 and holds 12 appointments. The new app declares version = 3 and registers only MIGRATION_2_3.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.missing.s1": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s2.title": "Room looks for a path from 1 to 3: the 1 → 2 arrow is missing",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s2.explain": "Room needs a chain of migrations joining 1 to 3. There is 2 → 3, but nothing starts at 1.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.missing.s2": "Room looks for a path from 1 to 3: the 1 → 2 arrow is missing",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s3.title": "IllegalStateException when opening the database",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s3.explain": "Room refuses to open and throws IllegalStateException. Every screen that reads the database crashes at once.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.missing.s3": "IllegalStateException when opening the database",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s4.title": "Crashes on every launch, until the user uninstalls",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.missing.s4.explain": "The file is still at v1, so the next launch hits the same error. The user's only way out is uninstalling, which deletes the 12 appointments anyway.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.missing.s4": "Crashes on every launch, until the user uninstalls",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s1.title": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s1.explain": "As before, but the builder adds fallbackToDestructiveMigration() \"just in case\".",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.destructive.s1": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s2.title": "No 1 → 2 path: Room falls back to destroying",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s2.explain": "Finding no path, Room does not crash; it follows the fallback.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.destructive.s2": "No 1 → 2 path: Room falls back to destroying",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s3.title": "Every table dropped, recreated with the v3 schema",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s3.explain": "The database is rebuilt empty at version 3. The 12 appointments are gone, including any booked offline and not yet sent to the server.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.destructive.s3": "Every table dropped, recreated with the v3 schema",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s4.title": "The app opens normally, with an empty list",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.destructive.s4.explain": "No crash, nothing in the log. The user just sees their appointments are gone.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.destructive.s4": "The app opens normally, with an empty list",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s1.title": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s1.explain": "The new app has AutoMigration(1, 2) and a hand-written MIGRATION_2_3: a path for every version ever shipped.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.complete.s1": "Update straight from version 1 to version 3",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s2.title": "Step 1 → 2: the automated migration adds the note column",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s2.explain": "Room compares the exported v1 and v2 schemas, sees a single nullable column added, and generates the ALTER TABLE itself. All 12 appointments remain.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.complete.s2": "Step 1 → 2: the automated migration adds the note column",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s3.title": "Step 2 → 3: the manual migration adds a column and fills it",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s3.explain": "The new statusCode column must take its value from the old status column. Room cannot guess that data transformation, so it is written by hand in SQL.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.complete.s3": "Step 2 → 3: the manual migration adds a column and fills it",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s4.title": "Room checks the schema matches v3, then opens",
  "track.storage.m.mig.s.complete.s4.explain": "After all migrations run, Room checks the actual schema matches the v3 schema it expects. It matches: the database opens with all 12 appointments.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.ev.complete.s4": "Room checks the schema matches v3, then opens",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.try": "Walk all four steps of each setup; watch how many appointments remain at the end.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.missing.s2": "Users do not upgrade in the order you release. Every version ever on the store needs a path to the latest one.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.missing.s3": "The Android docs say: if a migration path is missing, Room throws IllegalStateException. [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.missing.s4": "This only shows on devices still holding the old version; a developer's fresh install always works.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.destructive.s2": "fallbackToDestructiveMigration does not fix the missing path; it decides that losing data is acceptable.",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.destructive.s3": "The Android docs warn: fallbackToDestructiveMigration permanently deletes all data from the tables. [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.destructive.s4": "Only destroy data that is just a cache of the server. There are narrower variants: fallbackToDestructiveMigrationFrom(versions) and fallbackToDestructiveMigrationOnDowngrade(). [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.complete.s2": "Automated migrations rely on the generated schemas of both versions; if exportSchema is false, they fail. [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.complete.s3": "Manual migration: extend Migration(startVersion, endVersion), override migrate, register with addMigrations. The page advises writing full queries rather than constants. [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.m.mig.co.complete.s4": "From the page's test example: Room validates the schema once all migrations have run. [[src:ax-room-migrations]]",
  "track.storage.vz.tab.mg": "Version chain",
  "track.storage.vz.mg.cap": "Each box is a schema version; each arrow is a migration. The outlined box is the database version on the device right now.",
  "track.storage.vz.mg.v1": "appointment table: id, doctorId, time, status",
