  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s1.title": "Tap Book: call the server right away",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s1.explain": "The ViewModel calls api.book directly. There is no network, so the request never reaches the server.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.online.s1": "Tap Book: call the server right away",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s2.title": "IOException: no network",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s2.explain": "The call throws IOException. Nothing is written anywhere: not on the device, not on the server.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.online.s2": "IOException: no network",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s3.title": "Show the user an error",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s3.explain": "The screen says \"No network, try later\". Right for actions that must be confirmed at once, such as a bank transfer; for a booking, the user expects the app to remember it.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.online.s3": "Show the user an error",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s4.title": "The user closes the app: the booking never existed",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.online.s4.explain": "The user thinks it was booked, or forgets to retry. No trace of appointment #9 remains.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.online.s4": "The user closes the app: the booking never existed",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s1.title": "Save #9 to Room as PENDING",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s1.explain": "Local first: #9 goes into the appointment table with sync = PENDING. The UI reads a Flow from Room, so it shows at once.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.coroutine.s1": "Save #9 to Room as PENDING",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s2.title": "A coroutine retries every 30 seconds",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s2.explain": "A loop in viewModelScope calls the server and, on failure, delays and tries again.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.coroutine.s2": "A coroutine retries every 30 seconds",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s3.title": "Swipe the app away: the coroutine stops with it",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s3.explain": "viewModelScope is cancelled with the ViewModel; the process may be killed too. Nobody is left to send #9.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.coroutine.s3": "Swipe the app away: the coroutine stops with it",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s4.title": "#9 is stuck at PENDING",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.coroutine.s4.explain": "The appointment is still in Room, so it is not lost. But the server never gets it, until the user happens to reopen that exact screen.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.coroutine.s4": "#9 is stuck at PENDING",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s1.title": "Save #9 to Room, then enqueue work with WorkManager",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s1.explain": "Two lines: insert with sync = PENDING, then enqueueUniqueWork(\"sync\", KEEP, …) constrained to run only with a network. Both finish in milliseconds.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.lazy.s1": "Save #9 to Room, then enqueue work with WorkManager",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s2.title": "The app is killed; the work is kept",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s2.explain": "WorkManager has stored the request in its own SQLite database. Whether the app closes or the device reboots, the work is still there.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.lazy.s2": "The app is killed; the work is kept",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s3.title": "Network back: the worker reads the queue and sends",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s3.explain": "The network constraint is met and WorkManager runs SyncWorker, even with the app closed. The worker reads every PENDING row in Room and sends each one; the server answers 201.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.lazy.s3": "Network back: the worker reads the queue and sends",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s4.title": "Mark it SYNCED; next time the UI sees it",
  "track.storage.m.sync.s.lazy.s4.explain": "The worker updates #9 to SYNCED. Next time the app opens, the Flow from Room shows it confirmed. If sending fails, Result.retry() lets WorkManager try again with backoff.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.ev.lazy.s4": "Mark it SYNCED; next time the UI sees it",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.try": "Walk all four steps of each strategy; watch the queue table below the diagram.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.online.s2": "The offline-first page calls this an online-only write: write over the network first, update locally on success, otherwise throw to the caller. [[src:ax-offline-first-data]]",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.online.s3": "The same docs say: online-only suits near-real-time actions, such as a bank transfer. [[src:ax-offline-first-data]]",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.online.s4": "For data users expect the app to keep, online-only turns a lost connection into lost data.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.coroutine.s2": "Writing locally first is right; the mistake is letting the upload live in a coroutine tied to a screen.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.coroutine.s3": "The Android docs say: coroutines stop as soon as the app closes; WorkManager is for work that must run even if the app exits or the device restarts. [[src:ax-persistent-work]]",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.coroutine.s4": "The data is not lost but goes nowhere: this kind of bug only shows when server and device disagree.",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.lazy.s2": "The Android docs say: scheduled work is stored in an internally managed SQLite database and rescheduled across device reboots. [[src:ax-persistent-work]]",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.lazy.s3": "The Android docs say: the queue can be kept in Room and drained as persistent work with WorkManager; its example uses enqueueUniqueWork with KEEP and NetworkType.CONNECTED. [[src:ax-offline-first-data]]",
  "track.storage.m.sync.co.lazy.s4": "A lazy write: write locally first, then queue the network write at the earliest opportunity; the page calls it the right choice when data is critical. [[src:ax-offline-first-data]]",
